    {
      "id": "p0229-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The capital \"T\" in \"The Locket\" might seem like a simple typo at first, making it easy for players - and translators - to overlook its importance. What's more, the Japanese language lacks both uppercase writing and articles like \"a\" and \"the\". Had Underta/e's localization been rushed, this combination of language quirks could've easily led to a generic-sounding game phrase:",
        "raw": "The capital \"T\" in \"The Locket\" might seem like a simple typo at first, making\nit easy for players - and translators - to overlook its importance. What's more,\nthe Japanese language lacks both uppercase writing and articles like \"a\" and\n\"the\". Had Underta/e's localization been rushed, this combination of language\nquirks could've easily led to a generic-sounding game phrase:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09455966,
          0.4208,
          0.69639563,
          0.50604286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09254045,
          0.42008571,
          0.70941954,
          0.50711429
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          20,
          21,
          22,
          23,
          24
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "“The Locket”里大写的 T，乍看可能只是笔误，玩家和译者都很容易忽略它的重要性。日语既没有字母大小写，也没有 a、the 这样的冠词。假如《Undertale》的本地化赶工，这些语言差异凑在一起，很容易把它译成一句毫无特殊意味的游戏提示：",
        "status": "draft",
